From: SM-X910 postmarketOS port <gts9uwifi@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: snps-eusb2: match Samsung's downstream SM8550 init

The SM-X710 reaches DWC3 gadget mode with the upstream SM8550 eUSB2 PHY
sequence, but the host never sees a device: there is a USB device controller in
/sys/class/udc and no VID_0525 gadget at the other end of the cable (tests 013,
014, 017 - 30 minutes of USB monitoring).

Samsung's downstream SM8550 driver waits after asserting POR and programs
CPBIAS to one; the upstream sequence does neither.  This is exactly the fix the
SM-X910 port carries for the same symptom
(kernel/patches/match-samsung-sm8550-eusb2-phy-init.patch in
agcarbajo/ubuntu-galaxy-tab-s9-ultra), and the SM-X710 uses the same PHY - the
board DTS even models Samsung's eUSB2 repeater on i2c.

Signed-off-by: SM-X710 bring-up <gts9wifi@example.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c b/drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c
index af4fa17ac..27715b0fb 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c
@@ -372,6 +372,8 @@ static int qcom_snps_eusb2_hsphy_init(struct phy *p)
 				    CMN_CTRL_OVERRIDE_EN, CMN_CTRL_OVERRIDE_EN);
 
 	snps_eusb2_hsphy_write_mask(phy->base, QCOM_USB_PHY_UTMI_CTRL5, POR, POR);
+	/* Samsung's downstream SM8550 driver waits here before enabling the PHY. */
+	usleep_range(10, 20);
 
 	snps_eusb2_hsphy_write_mask(phy->base, QCOM_USB_PHY_HS_PHY_CTRL_COMMON0,
 				    PHY_ENABLE | RETENABLEN, PHY_ENABLE | RETENABLEN);
@@ -391,7 +393,7 @@ static int qcom_snps_eusb2_hsphy_init(struct phy *p)
 
 	snps_eusb2_hsphy_write_mask(phy->base, QCOM_USB_PHY_CFG_CTRL_1,
 				    PHY_CFG_PLL_CPBIAS_CNTRL_MASK,
-				    FIELD_PREP(PHY_CFG_PLL_CPBIAS_CNTRL_MASK, 0x0));
+				    FIELD_PREP(PHY_CFG_PLL_CPBIAS_CNTRL_MASK, 0x1));
 
 	snps_eusb2_hsphy_write_mask(phy->base, QCOM_USB_PHY_CFG_CTRL_4,
 				    PHY_CFG_PLL_INT_CNTRL_MASK,
